# Melodia Toon Film — attribute policy
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# --------------------
# Two people editing M_Master_Toon_Universal.uasset on this repo, with git
# treating it as TEXT, produces a merged .uasset that Unreal cannot open. The
# corruption is silent and unrecoverable. Declaring the binary types below is
# the fix; it costs nothing and it is the single highest-value file in the repo
# for a group.
#
# THE SPLIT, AND WHY IT IS NOT "LFS EVERYTHING"
# ---------------------------------------------
# This repo's 29 .uasset/.umap files total ~0.4 MB. Putting them behind LFS
# would force every teammate to install git-lfs to open a material, for no
# benefit - and migrating the ones already committed means rewriting history,
# which this project does not do casually.
#
# So: heavy ART (`.blend`, `.fbx`, `.exr`, renders) is LFS, because that is the
# weight that will actually grow and the weight that actually breaks clones.
# Engine packages are declared BINARY (no merge attempt) but stay plain objects.
#
# GitHub's free LFS tier is 1 GB storage / 1 GB bandwidth per month. If the
# group exhausts that on repeated clones, the documented alternative is the one
# the source project already uses: keep bulk art out of git and share it from a
# drive. See Docs/GROUP_WORKFLOW.md.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- text sources
# Normalised to LF so the group's Windows/macOS/Linux checkouts do not churn
# every file on every pull.
*.py        text eol=lf
*.md        text eol=lf
*.json      text eol=lf
*.csv       text eol=lf
*.ps1       text eol=crlf
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.ini       text eol=lf
*.uproject  text eol=lf
*.gitignore text eol=lf

# ------------------------------------------------- engine packages (binary)
# `-text` stops the text merge. `-diff` keeps git from rendering a bogus diff.
# WITHOUT LFS on purpose - see the note above.
*.uasset     -text -diff
*.umap       -text -diff

# ------------------------------------------------------- heavy art (LFS)
*.blend      filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.blend1     filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.fbx        filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.exr        filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.hdr        filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.mov        filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.mp4        filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.wav        filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.png        filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.tga        filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.psd        filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.ztl        filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.spp        filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# ------------------------------------------------------------- generated files
# These are regenerated from the Python builders; a merge conflict in them is
# meaningless, so never attempt one.
/Content/__ExternalActors__/  linguist-generated=true
/Content/__ExternalObjects__/ linguist-generated=true
